(7578475, 1216379, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Clever rotation of this imagery creates a conceptual work with lots of symbology- An awakening; a ''rebirth'' is present in this photo. To me, the swimmer looks like she is about to break free from the blue realm and open her eyes to a ''new world''.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Clever rotation of this imagery creates a conceptual work with lots of symbology- An awakening; a ''rebirth'' is present in this photo. To me, the swimmer looks like she is about to break free from the blue realm and open her eyes to a ''new world''.', '2018-07-07 23:20:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(7578476, 1216679, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Beautiful minimalist composition that explores the blue color found within the folds and shapes of paper. A pleasing study of lines and curves this photo draws the eye in.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. Beautiful minimalist composition that explores the blue color found within the folds and shapes of paper. A pleasing study of lines and curves this photo draws the eye in.', '2018-07-07 23:23:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(7578484, 1216610, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>There is alot of beautiful blues in this still life composition. Lighting is fantastic and as that it can be challenging to get good light and definition to to glass - well done on that aspect! I do have Two critiques which is the composition is too busy and the arrangement of glasses is too linear. The swirling backdrop with patterns and varying hues in light and dark actually competes and distracts attention away from your main subject. A background that complements the subject with distracting would be better. The other suggestion is by layering or stacking the objects in a grouping you can add visual interest with the eye traveling around to and fro from front to back to discover all the interesting shapes, patterns and intersecting lines.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment. There is alot of beautiful blues in this still life composition. Lighting is fantastic and as that it can be challenging to get good light and definition to to glass - well done on that aspect! I do have Two critiques which is the composition is too busy and the arrangement of glasses is too linear. The swirling backdrop with patterns and varying hues in light and dark actually competes and distracts attention away from your main subject. A background that complements the subject with distracting would be better. The other suggestion is by layering or stacking the objects in a grouping you can add visual interest with the eye traveling around to and fro from front to back to discover all the interesting shapes, patterns and intersecting lines.', '2018-07-07 23:35:53.000000', NULL, 1),
