(7579714, 1216987, 111937, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by JulietNN:</b></div><hr/><i> Brilliant shot, very crisp and clean. I love your smoke bomb. What type did you use?  I tried one, and ended up setting fire to my model lol. <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1216798" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/87808/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1216798.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/87808/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1216798.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/87808/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1216798.jpg"/></a> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/><a href="https://www.ansgear.com/Paintball_Smoke_Grenades_s/4859.htm" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Smoke Bomb</a> <br/> <br/>This is what I used. It comes in different size, I used the smallest one which last for 45 sec. bigger size lasts longer but gets hot too ... I did notice the color from smoke bombs do get on the clothes which is hard to remove .... esp in white clothes.<br/> <br/>Below is some more pics using smoke bomb ....<br/> <br/><a href="https://instagram.com/p/Bj8EEFfHEET/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">smoke bomb 1</a> <br/> <br/><a href="https://instagram.com/p/Bh7lcf6HDes/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Smoke Bomb 2</a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2018-07-09 14:17:24.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by JulietNN: Brilliant shot, very crisp and clean. I love your smoke bomb. What type did you use?  I tried one, and ended up setting fire to my model lol.    Smoke Bomb  This is what I used. It comes in different size, I used the smallest one which last for 45 sec. bigger size lasts longer but gets hot too ... I did notice the color from smoke bombs do get on the clothes which is hard to remove .... esp in white clothes. Below is some more pics using smoke bomb .... smoke bomb 1  Smoke Bomb 2', '2018-07-09 14:59:39.000000', '2018-07-09 15:17:24.000000', 0),
(7579725, 1216565, 16106, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the explanation of the process, your diligence was rewarded.<br/> This was a 7 for me and would have been higher but for that lable on the wine bottle. It is the source of the brightest whites and the greatest contrasts in the image (and letters always pull the eye), but it doesn''t contribute to the overalll image at all. Had you turned the bottle so the lable''s impact was diminished (or better yet soaked it off) the bird and the flower would have had their rightful place as the magnets to the eye. With the subtle reflections on the bottle and the blueberries in harmony.<br/>PS..spraying the bottle with artist''s fixative, or hairspray will diffuse reflections giving blurry highlights and lines instead of crisp reflections of whatever is behind the photographer. <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2018-07-09 14:39:41.</i></td>', 'Thanks for the explanation of the process, your diligence was rewarded. This was a 7 for me and would have been higher but for that lable on the wine bottle. It is the source of the brightest whites and the greatest contrasts in the image (and letters always pull the eye), but it doesn''t contribute to the overalll image at all. Had you turned the bottle so the lable''s impact was diminished (or better yet soaked it off) the bird and the flower would have had their rightful place as the magnets to the eye. With the subtle reflections on the bottle and the blueberries in harmony.PS..spraying the bottle with artist''s fixative, or hairspray will diffuse reflections giving blurry highlights and lines instead of crisp reflections of whatever is behind the photographer. ', '2018-07-09 15:35:46.000000', '2018-07-09 15:39:41.000000', 0),
